{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1774454922,"nonce":"CfEAbXoALFj68YFYxaITaY6uP18=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOK4fCvM72j9Ci","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/12","origin":"github"},"title":"Rename network device identities to match hostname aliases","message":"## Summary\n\nThe MikroTik WiFi bridge devices and Teltonika routers currently have factory-default or non-descriptive hostnames (e.g., the IzzyBoat OmniTIK shows `EB160`). When SSH'd into these devices, the prompt doesn't indicate which device you're on, making troubleshooting confusing — especially when jumping between multiple devices.\n\n## Proposed Change\n\nRename device identities to match the hostname aliases used in our network configuration.\n\n### MikroTik devices (RouterOS `/system identity`)\n\n| Device | Current Identity | Proposed Identity |\n|--------|-----------------|-------------------|\n| IzzyBoat OmniTIK | `EB160` | `wifi_izzyboat` |\n| IzzyBoat SXTsq | (check) | `wifi_izzyboat_operator` |\n| BizzyBoat OmniTIK | (check) | `wifi_bizzyboat` |\n| BizzyBoat SXTsq | (check) | `wifi_bizzyboat_operator` |\n\n### Teltonika routers (hostname in System → Administration)\n\n| Device | Proposed Hostname |\n|--------|-------------------|\n| IzzyBoat router | `router_izzyboat` |\n| BizzyBoat router | `router_bizzyboat` |\n| Operator router | `router_operator` |\n\nThis makes prompts immediately identify which device you're connected to:\n```\n[admin@wifi_izzyboat] \u003e\nroot@router_bizzyboat:~#\n```\n\n## Steps\n\n1. Connect to each device\n2. MikroTik: `/system identity set name=\u003cnew_name\u003e`\n3. Teltonika: Set hostname via web UI (System → Administration) or UCI\n4. Verify prompt updates\n5. Document the changes\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.6`","files":null}]}